        "html": "<li><div class=\"wp-block-latest-posts__featured-image alignright\"><a href=\"/rcj-ir-soccer-ball-2026-changes-announced/\" aria-label=\"RCJ IR Soccer Ball &#8211; 2026 Changes Announced\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"300\" height=\"221\" src=\"/wp-content/uploads/2025/01/close-300x221.jpg\" class=\"attachment-medium size-medium wp-post-image\" alt=\"\" style=\"\" srcset=\"/wp-content/uploads/2025/01/close-300x221.jpg 300w, /wp-content/uploads/2025/01/close-1024x753.jpg 1024w, /wp-content/uploads/2025/01/close-768x565.jpg 768w, /wp-content/uploads/2025/01/close-1536x1130.jpg 1536w, /wp-content/uploads/2025/01/close-2048x1507.jpg 2048w, /wp-content/uploads/2025/01/close-408x300.jpg 408w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 300px) 100vw, 300px\" /></a></div><a class=\"wp-block-latest-posts__post-title\" href=\"/rcj-ir-soccer-ball-2026-changes-announced/\">RCJ IR Soccer Ball &#8211; 2026 Changes Announced</a><div class=\"wp-block-latest-posts__post-author\">by RoboCup Admin</div><time datetime=\"2025-01-31T05:51:45-05:00\" class=\"wp-block-latest-posts__post-date\">January 31, 2025</time><div class=\"wp-block-latest-posts__post-excerpt\">Soccer Lightweight Ball changes in 2026 Starting in 2026, Lightweight Soccer will be moving to a new IR Ball. The key difference with this ball is the size change from 74mm to 42mm diameter, which is the same size as the Open League’s passive ball. This ball is Open-Source, so anyone can produce one from &hellip;</div></li>"
      },
